---
import DocLayout from '../layouts/DocLayout.astro';
import { siteName, supportEmail } from '../config/site';
---

<DocLayout
  title={`Privacy - ${siteName}`}
  description={`How ${siteName} handles your files and data. Short answer: it doesn't, everything runs on your device.`}
  heading="Privacy"
  updated="Last updated August 2026"
>
  <Fragment slot="lead">
    {siteName} is a static site with no backend. As of the date above every tool runs inside your browser,
    so there is no server to receive your files. You don't have to take our word for it: the whole thing
    is open source, so you can read exactly what any tool does.
  </Fragment>

  <section>
    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <p>Nothing. No accounts, no analytics, no tracking scripts, no advertising, no cookies.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Hosting</h2>
    <p>
      A third-party CDN serves the site and, like any host, may record standard access logs: IP
      address, page requested, timestamp, user agent, and similar technical data. We add no
      analytics on top and don't use these to identify anyone. Fonts are self-hosted, and no
      third-party font, analytics, or advertising service is loaded.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Depending on where you live you may have rights to access, correct, or delete personal data
      held about you. In practice we hold none unless you've emailed us.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      <a href={`mailto:${supportEmail}`}>{supportEmail}</a>. Emailing us means we receive your
      address and whatever you include, used only to reply and never added to a list.
    </p>
  </section>
</DocLayout>
